{"id":"u-98207135-dd23-48a5-9c30-607cf45b55c3","src":"community","title":"Texas Method #2","author":"IronReep3r","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/bKDPxG-texas-method-2","desc":"TEXAS METHOD VOLUME DAY\nMonday is the texas method workout with the most volume, i.e. the most total sets. The original programme calls for 5×5 squats, 5×5 bench press and 4x8 barbell rows. These are typically performed at 70-90% of your previous Friday’s 5 rep max.\n\nTEXAS METHOD RECOVERY DAY\nWednesday is the texas method workout based around recovery, so you’ll perform a much lower volume of work (less sets) and the weights you use will also be lighter. Typically you’ll lift weights that are 80-90% of what you did on Monday.\n\nTEXAS METHOD INTENSITY DAY\nFriday is the texas method workout that pushes up the intensity, i.e. has you lift heavier weights. The program calls for a 5 rep max in the squat, bench or press, and deadlift. You’ll have to work hard and focus, but you’ll only have to do one challenging set.\n\nPROGRESSION \nThe most common way of progressing on TM is to increase 5RM done on intensity day with 2.5 kg, given you completed last weeks 1x5.\n\nHere is an helpful article on how to do, and modify  the program: https://www.scribd.com/document/458458072/Justin-Lascek-The-Texas-Method-Part-1","level":["Novice","Intermediate"],"goals":["Strength","Muscle"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":13,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-10-27T22:16:10.809Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Squat (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8,"x":5}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":5,"rpe":8,"x":5}]},{"n":"Bent Over Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lying Tricep Extension (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Bicep Curl (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Squa